    "answer": "Based on the provided academic context, here are a few regulations mentioned:\n\n1. Students joining the B.Tech. Programme shall have to complete the programme in a stipulated time frame of 8 years from the date of joining.\n2. Students joining the B.Tech. Programme in the third semester directly through Lateral Entry Scheme (LES) shall have to complete the programme in a stipulated time frame of 6 years from the date of joining.\n3. The Semester End Examinations (SEE) in all the subjects shall be conducted at the end of each semester for all the eight semesters.\n4. A student shall be eligible for promotion to the next semester if they satisfy the attendance requirements.\n5. Detained and break-in study candidates are not eligible for the award of First Class with Distinction.\n6. The performance of a student in each semester shall be evaluated subject-wise with a maximum of 100 marks for theory and 100 marks for practical subjects.",
